stored as a binary tree in an array.","3":"<code>before(x, y)</code> says whether <code>x</code> belongs nearer the root than <code>y</code>.","4":"How many pins the heap currently holds.","7":"Shorthand for the item array.","8":"Place the new item at the bottom of the tree.","9":"<code>i</code> is where the new item currently sits.","10":"Bubble it up until it reaches the root.","11":"<code>p</code> is the parent slot of <code>i</code>.","12":"Parent already belongs above it: the order is restored.","13":"Swap the item above its parent.","14":"Continue from the parent's slot.","19":"Remember the root item and remove the last one to refill the root.","20":"Only rearrange if items remain.","21":"Move the last item to the root.","22":"<code>i</code> is where that item currently sits.","23":"Sink it until neither child belongs above it.","24":"Slots of the two children of <code>i</code>.","25":"<code>m</code> will be whichever of the three belongs highest.","26":"The left child belongs above it.","27":"The right child belongs above both.","28":"The item is already in place.","29":"Swap it below that child.","30":"Continue from that child's slot.","33":"The removed root item, here the farthest pin kept.","36":"A copy of every pin still in the heap, in no particular order.","41":"A max-heap on squared distance, so the farthest kept pin is always at the root.","42":"Consider each pin in turn.","43":"Add the pin, keyed by its squared distance to the center.","44":"One pin too many: the farthest kept one cannot be among the <code>k</code> closest.","46":"The heap now holds the <code>k</code> closest pins; drop the distance and return coordinates."},"py":{"3":"Min-heap on negated squared distance, so the farthest kept pin sits at the root.","4":"Consider each pin in turn.","5":"Add the pin with its distance negated, turning Python's min-heap into a max-heap.","6":"Holding one pin more than <code>k</code>.","7":"Drop the farthest kept pin; it cannot be among the <code>k</code> closest.","8":"The heap holds the <code>k</code> closest pins; return just their coordinates."}}}],"expected":[[0,-2],[4,4]],"compare":{"check":"(args, got, expected) => {\n      const [pts, k] = args;\n      if (!Array.isArray(got) || got.length !== k) return false;\n      const d = p => p[0] * p[0] + p[1] * p[1];\n      const left = new Map();\n      for (const p of pts) left.set(p[0] + \",\" + p[1], (left.get(p[0] + \",\" + p[1]) || 0) + 1);\n      for (const p of got) {\n        if (!Array.isArray(p) || p.length !== 2) return false;\n        const key = p[0] + \",\" + p[1], c = left.get(key) || 0;\n        if (!c) return false; // not an input pin, or returned twice\n        left.set(key, c - 1);\n      }\n      const best = pts.map(d).sort((a, b) => a - b).slice(0, k);\n      const mine = got.map(d).sort((a, b) => a - b);\n      return best.every((v, i) => v === mine[i]);\n    }"}}